<DocsLayout
	title="Get Started"
	description="Guideline step by step to start taking advantage of Bravo Design System."
	currentPath="/getting-started"
>
	<h1 id="getstarted-heading">Get Started</h1>
	<p>
		Guideline step by step to start taking advantage of Bravo Design System.
	</p>

	<h2>1. Configure Tokens</h2>
	<p>
		Start by customizing the design tokens to match your brand and product needs.
		Tokens define foundational design choices such as color, spacing, and typography.
		You’ll find and edit these in the <strong>docs/tokens</strong> folder separated by Core, Semantic, Composite and Theme .json files.
	</p>
	<p><a href="/foundations/tokens">Tokens</a></p>

	<h2>2. Define Vision and Foundations</h2>
	<p>
		Set your organization’s design vision, voice, and core principles. These
		foundations guide decision-making and ensure a cohesive visual and
		communication style across your products.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="/vision/design-principles">Design principles</a></li>
		<li><a href="/vision/voice-and-tone">Voice &amp; tone</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. Build and Document Components</h2>
	<p>
		Develop reusable UI components that follow your foundational guidelines and
		design tokens. Document usage, states, and accessibility considerations
		clearly for your team.
	</p>
		<p><a href="/components/button">Components</a></p>

	<h2>4. Establish Patterns</h2>
	<p>
		Create and document reusable UI patterns—such as navigation, forms, and
		layout structures—that help your team build consistent, user-friendly
		experiences.
	</p>
	<p><a href="/patterns/example-empty-state">See patterns specs</a></p>

	<h2>5. Set Up Governance</h2>
	<p>
		Define how your design system will evolve and be maintained. Include
		contribution guidelines, versioning policies, and decision-making processes
		to keep your system robust and future-proof.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="/governance/quality-bar">Governance and quality bar</a></li>
		<li><a href="/governance/contribution-model">Contribution process</a></li>
		<li><a href="/governance/decisions-backlog">Backlog &amp; decisions</a></li>
	</ul>
</DocsLayout>
